 # Mate Terminal
 ## Overview
-Mate Terminal provides a graphic interface of charaters system. The main interface as shown in Fig 1.
 
-![Fig 1 Mate Terminal-big](image/1.png)
+The terminal is the medium through which the Kylin system operates using system commands. It provides a character system window in a graphical interface. Interaction with the system can be achieved by typing system instructions in the terminal window.
+
 <br>
 
-## Basic Function
-- Charaters system
+### Opening method
+
+- **â€œopening menuâ€**![](image/icon1.png)>**â€œmate-terminalâ€**![](image/icon2.png)
+- Right-click on an empty area of the desktop > Open the right-click menu bar on the desktop > selected**â€œOpen terminalâ€**![](image/icon2.png)
+- Select the folder in the File Manager or right-click in the blank area > Open the right-click menu bar > selected**â€œOpen terminalâ€**![](image/icon2.png)
+- **â€œtaskbarâ€**>**â€œsearchâ€** ![](image/icon3.png)>**â€œmate-terminalâ€** ![](image/icon2.png)> selected**â€œopenâ€**
+
+![Fig 1 Terminal-Day Mode](image/1.png)
+
+![Fig 2 Terminal-Night mode](image/2.png)
+
+### Basic Function
+After opening the terminal, based on the current user's permissions, you can directly input the corresponding system commands using the keyboard in the terminal window and press Enter. The terminal will judge the instructions and output the corresponding prompts. Multiple terminal Windows can be opened simultaneously for operation.
 
-- Execute commands and scripts
 
+The basic functions provided by the terminal are:
+
+- Charaters system
+- Execute commands and scripts
 - Use the applications/services only running in terminal
 
-<br>
+![Fig 3 Terminal window](image/3.png)
 
-## Advanced Function
-### Single Settings
-Only effective in the current window, and invalid after closing.
+Take the operation window as shown in the above pictureï¼Œkylin@kylin-pc:/opt$ï¼Œamong them:
 
-- Title
+- kylinï¼šThe username for logging into the system
+- kylin-pcï¼šComputer name
+- /optï¼šThe path when the terminal is currently opened
 
-Click "Terminal" > "Set Title" to modify the current window's name, as shown in Fig 2.
+#### Shortcut Key
 
-![Fig 2 Title](image/2.png)
+The following table lists some commonly used shortcut keys for terminal operationsï¼ŒMore shortcuts can be seen or modified by "Edit" > "Keyboard Shortcuts".
 
-- Charater Encoding
+| Shortcut          | Function           |
+|--------------|--------------|
+| Ctrl+Alt+T   | Open a new ternimal window      |
+| Ctrl+Shift+T | Open a new tab in the current terminal window |
+| Ctrl+D       | Close the current window/tab   |
+| F11          | Fullscreen/Quit Fullscreen    |
 
-Click "Terminal" > "Set Charater Encoding" to adjust it.
+### Advanced Function
+Advanced Settings can be configured through the terminal menu bar options. For detailed function descriptions of the menu bar, please refer to the menu bar.
 
-![Fig 3 Encoding-big](image/3.png)
+#### Single Settings
 
-It provides multiple encodings in "Add or Remove".
